.Simultaneously learning the sparsity of convolution and fully connected layers is beneficial in amortizing the training cost and in performing holistic trade - off among accuracy , classification speed , and model size .However , when targeting no accuracy loss from sparse models , we find that using the same regularization parameters across all layers tends to provide a high sparsity on fully connected ( fc ) layers but not enough sparsity on convolution layers to obtain speedups from sparse convolutions .Therefore , trading off a small increase in model size of fc layers for a large speedup of convolution layers can be often beneficial for holistically optimizing the accuracy - speed - size of CNN .Thelower convolution layers such as conv 1 in AlexNet are much harder to sparsify than higher layers such as conv 2 and above unless we can tolerate a large accuracy drop .Specifically , we use weight decay 1e - 5 , 5e - 5 , and 6e - 5 , for FC decay multiplier 1 , 0. 1 , and 0.0 1 , respectively . among accuracy , speed , and model size .Our Holistic SparseCNN achieves a classification speed of 2, 3 7 1 images per second on BDW , without accuracy drop compared to the reference Caffe model .With
